    Don't fail ingest with 500 if a media URL can't be fetched (#8339)
    
    If the ingest service could not fetch content from a URL a client
    specified, e.g. because the host was unreachable or responded with an
    error, the client got an HTTP 500, Opencast logged a full stack trace
    and the failed job put the ingest service into the WARNING state.
    
    A URL which cannot be fetched is a problem of the request, though. The
    ingest service now throws a dedicated MediaFetchException in this case,
    marks the job as failed because of its data, which does not affect the
    service state, and the REST endpoints respond with HTTP 400 and a single
    warning in the log. Failures to store the downloaded content are still
    treated as problems of the service.
    
    This also fixes a NullPointerException for URLs without file name
    extension and without Content-Disposition header.
    
    Fixes #8322
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    This should return an 500 internal server error + log a stack trace
    without this patch and a 400 bad request with this patch:
    ```
    curl -i -u admin:opencast https://develop.opencast.org/ingest/addMediaPackage/fast  -F 'flavor=presenter/source' -F 'mediaUri=https://invalid.example.com/video.mp4'  -F title=Test
    ```
    
